{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "fbb2deb0-d1c8-4f48-bed9-64e6a30a3f1c",
    "name": "payment-flow",
    "description": "Local walk-through of the payment-flow API.\n\nImport the **payment-flow local** environment too, then run the folders top to bottom (Collection Runner makes the scripts fire in order).\n\n1. `POST /checkout-intents` creates an order and fills in the variables the other requests use.\n2. Folder **01 Checkout** shows retries, payload conflicts and 10 concurrent checkouts.\n3. Folder **02 Webhooks** shows apply, duplicate delivery, a stale failure, an event-id conflict and 10 concurrent deliveries.\n4. Folder **03 Read** shows the status endpoints.\n\nStart the service first: `docker compose up --build`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 Checkout",
      "description": "Idempotent checkout intents. Run the requests in order.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Create checkout intent (expect 201)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Fresh identifiers for every run of this collection.",
                  "const suffix = Date.now().toString().slice(-8);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('order_reference', 'POSTMAN-ORDER-' + suffix);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('evt_succeeded', 'evt_pm_success_' + suffix);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('evt_failed', 'evt_pm_fail_' + suffix);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('evt_parallel', 'evt_pm_parallel_' + suffix);",
                  "console.log('using order reference', pm.collectionVariables.get('order_reference'));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('created is true', () => pm.expect(body.created).to.be.true);",
                  "pm.test('status starts as pending', () => pm.expect(body.order.status).to.eql('pending'));",
                  "pm.test('amount is stored as integer minor units', () => pm.expect(body.order.amountMinor).to.eql(2599));",
                  "",
                  "// Keep the id so the requests in folder 03 can use it. Collection",
                  "// variables only: writing to the environment would leave values behind",
                  "// that shadow these on the next run.",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('order_id', body.order.id);",
                  "console.log('order', body.order);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/checkout-intents",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "checkout-intents"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates the order and stores its id in the collection and environment variables.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"orderReference\": \"{{order_reference}}\",\n  \"amountMinor\": 2599,\n  \"currency\": \"EUR\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Retry with identical payload (expect 200, no duplicate)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('created is false', () => pm.expect(body.created).to.be.false);",
                  "pm.test('returns the existing order', () => pm.expect(body.order.id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('order_id')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/checkout-intents",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "checkout-intents"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The business order reference is the idempotency key, so this returns the same order instead of creating a second one.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"orderReference\": \"{{order_reference}}\",\n  \"amountMinor\": 2599,\n  \"currency\": \"EUR\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Retry with a different amount (expect 409, nothing changed)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('error code', () => pm.expect(body.error.code).to.eql('checkout_payload_conflict'));",
                  "pm.test('reports the conflicting field', () => pm.expect(body.error.details.conflictingFields).to.eql(['amountMinor']));",
                  "pm.test('stored amount is untouched', () => pm.expect(body.error.details.existingOrder.amountMinor).to.eql(2599));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/checkout-intents",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "checkout-intents"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Reusing a reference with a changed amount is rejected; the stored order is not modified.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"orderReference\": \"{{order_reference}}\",\n  \"amountMinor\": 9999,\n  \"currency\": \"EUR\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 Webhooks",
      "description": "Provider events applied exactly once. Run after folder 01.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. payment.succeeded (expect applied)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('event is applied', () => pm.expect(body.applied).to.be.true);",
                  "pm.test('outcome is applied', () => pm.expect(body.outcome).to.eql('applied'));",
                  "pm.test('not a duplicate', () => pm.expect(body.duplicate).to.be.false);",
                  "pm.test('order is now succeeded', () => pm.expect(body.order.status).to.eql('succeeded'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/webhooks/payment-provider",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "webhooks",
                "payment-provider"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Moves the order from pending to succeeded.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"id\": \"{{evt_succeeded}}\",\n  \"type\": \"payment.succeeded\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-01-05T10:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"orderReference\": \"{{order_reference}}\",\n    \"providerPaymentId\": \"pay_postman_1\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Same event again (duplicate, no second apply)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('flagged as duplicate', () => pm.expect(body.duplicate).to.be.true);",
                  "pm.test('not applied again', () => pm.expect(body.applied).to.be.false);",
                  "pm.test('deliveryCount is 2', () => pm.expect(body.deliveryCount).to.eql(2));",
                  "pm.test('order still succeeded', () => pm.expect(body.order.status).to.eql('succeeded'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/webhooks/payment-provider",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "webhooks",
                "payment-provider"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The provider never saw the first response and retries: nothing is applied twice.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"id\": \"{{evt_succeeded}}\",\n  \"type\": \"payment.succeeded\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-01-05T10:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"orderReference\": \"{{order_reference}}\",\n    \"providerPaymentId\": \"pay_postman_1\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Stale payment.failed after success (ignored_terminal)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('outcome is ignored_terminal', () => pm.expect(body.outcome).to.eql('ignored_terminal'));",
                  "pm.test('not applied', () => pm.expect(body.applied).to.be.false);",
                  "pm.test('different event id, so not a duplicate', () => pm.expect(body.duplicate).to.be.false);",
                  "pm.test('order stays succeeded', () => pm.expect(body.order.status).to.eql('succeeded'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/webhooks/payment-provider",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "webhooks",
                "payment-provider"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Success is terminal: a late failure for the same payment cannot regress the order.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"id\": \"{{evt_failed}}\",\n  \"type\": \"payment.failed\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"orderReference\": \"{{order_reference}}\",\n    \"providerPaymentId\": \"pay_postman_1\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Same event id, different payload (event_id_conflict)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('outcome is event_id_conflict', () => pm.expect(body.outcome).to.eql('event_id_conflict'));",
                  "pm.test('the changed payload is not applied', () => pm.expect(body.applied).to.be.false);",
                  "pm.test('order stays succeeded', () => pm.expect(body.order.status).to.eql('succeeded'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/webhooks/payment-provider",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "webhooks",
                "payment-provider"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The provider reuses an event id for different content: counted, acknowledged, never processed twice.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"id\": \"{{evt_succeeded}}\",\n  \"type\": \"payment.failed\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"orderReference\": \"{{order_reference}}\",\n    \"providerPaymentId\": \"pay_postman_1\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Event for an unknown order (order_not_found)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('outcome is order_not_found', () => pm.expect(body.outcome).to.eql('order_not_found'));",
                  "pm.test('nothing applied', () => pm.expect(body.applied).to.be.false);",
                  "pm.test('no order in the response', () => pm.expect(body.order).to.eql(null));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/webhooks/payment-provider",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "webhooks",
                "payment-provider"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The event is stored and applied on a later delivery once the order exists.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"id\": \"evt_pm_unknown_1\",\n  \"type\": \"payment.succeeded\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"orderReference\": \"ORDER-DOES-NOT-EXIST-1\",\n    \"providerPaymentId\": \"pay_postman_2\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "03 Read",
      "description": "Order status lookups.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get order by business reference",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('reference matches', () => pm.expect(body.order.orderReference).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('order_reference')));",
                  "pm.test('amount is unchanged', () => pm.expect(body.order.amountMinor).to.eql(2599));",
                  "console.log('order', body.order);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/orders/{{order_reference}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders",
                "{{order_reference}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": ""
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get order by id",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('id matches', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().order.id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('order_id')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/orders/id/{{order_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders",
                "id",
                "{{order_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": ""
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Unknown reference (expect 404)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('404 Not Found', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
                  "pm.test('error code', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.code).to.eql('not_found'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/orders/ORDER-DOES-NOT-EXIST-1",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders",
                "ORDER-DOES-NOT-EXIST-1"
              ]
            },
            "description": ""
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Malformed id (expect 400)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('error code', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.code).to.eql('invalid_request'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/orders/id/not-a-uuid",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "orders",
                "id",
                "not-a-uuid"
              ]
            },
            "description": ""
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('database reachable', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().database).to.eql('reachable'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": ""
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
